invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: message_mod_prime multiplies the message's high limbs by R^2 where R^3 is
  needed, so the message is reduced to high + low * R modulo the prime
  where high * R + low is wanted, and each half is the power of another
  number. The signature's check refuses the result, so nothing wrong
  leaves; every signature fails. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test signs under four
  keys and requires the ladder's bytes.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_mont_mul(high, high, r3, mod);
--- new
    rsa_mont64_mont_mul(high, high, mod->r2, mod);
